answer.worked:
The angle $\frac{2\pi}{3}$ lies in the second quadrant, where sine is positive.
$$\begin{align*}
\sin \frac{2\pi}{3} &= \sin \left(\pi - \frac{\pi}{3}\right) \\
&= \sin \frac{\pi}{3} \\
&= \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}
\end{align*}$$
